course: dictionary
lesson: 5166
title: Islam, a proper name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Islam is a proper noun. It is the name of a religion, so it begins with a capital letter, just like London or Ella. When you read it, look at the words around it to find out what it means.
explain: «Islam is a faith in one God, called Allah in Arabic; its followers are Muslims.» The clue is in the second half: followers are Muslims, so Islam must be the faith that Muslims follow. Try it: swap in "faith" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Islam can also mean the wider Muslim world, including its people and culture. «The Qur'an is the holy book of Islam» uses it in the first sense, as the religion. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the whole sentence and asking what fits.
fact: Islam is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Islam» means the religion of Muslims, who believe in one God, called Allah in Arabic.
fact: «Islam» can also mean the Muslim world and its people and culture.
fact: Muslims pray in a «mosque» and their holy book is the «Qur'an», which is recited in Arabic.
fact: The Five Pillars of Islam are five key practices of the faith, including prayer and fasting in Ramadan.
exercise: «Islam is a faith in one God, called Allah in Arabic.» What is Islam? | A country in Africa | *A religion, the faith of Muslims | A type of school subject | A kind of food eaten at Eid
exercise: Why does Islam start with a capital letter? | Because it is a long word | Because it is the first word in every sentence | *Because it is a proper noun, the name of a religion | Because it is written in Arabic
exercise: «Muslims pray in a mosque, standing shoulder to shoulder.» What is a Muslim? | A holy book | A special festival | A type of building for prayer | *A person who follows Islam
test:
«The Qur'an is the holy book of Islam.» What is the Qur'an? | A festival called Eid | *The holy book of Islam | The name of a mosque | A prayer said five times a day
Islam can mean the Muslim world and its people and culture. Which sentence uses Islam in this wider sense? | «Islam is a faith in one God.» | *«The history of Islam is long and rich, with many cultures.» | «Islam means submission to God.» | «Muslims pray in a mosque.»
exam: Which statement about Islam is true? | *Islam is a religion that believes in one God, called Allah in Arabic | Islam is a festival called Eid | Islam is a mosque | Islam is a holy book
